# Generated data artifacts -- all reproducible by re-running src/*.py against the
# ASVspoof datasets. Also, manifests/ and splits/ embed absolute local filesystem
# paths (E:\ASVspoof data\..., see src/config.py), which are meaningless outside
# this machine -- another reason not to version them.
manifests/
splits/
features/
models/

# results/: the small summaries, aggregate tables and figures ARE tracked (same
# rationale as EDA/ -- small, and they are the thing you actually want to read in
# the repo). Only the bulky per-file score dumps are excluded: ~2.3MB each today,
# and Phase 7's 2021 versions will carry 721,332 rows. Those regenerate in seconds
# by re-scoring an already-saved model -- fitting is the slow part, not scoring.
#
# The leading ** matters: results are now nested per phase (and per run in Phase 6),
# and a single * does NOT cross directory separators -- so `results/*dev_scores*.csv`
# silently failed to match results/phase6/<tag>/dev_scores.csv.
**/dev_scores*.csv

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# Environments (this project's venv lives outside the repo, in a sibling folder,
# but ignore the common local names anyway in case that ever changes)
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Editor / tool-local state (machine-specific, e.g. hardcoded interpreter paths)
.vscode/
.claude/
.idea/

# Exported session transcripts. Kept locally as a working reference for writing up
# the thesis, but not published: they are raw conversation logs, they duplicate what
# PROGRESS_REPORT.md records deliberately, and they can be regenerated at any time
# from ~/.claude/projects/<project>/<session-id>.jsonl via export_conversation.py.
conversation_export/

# OS junk
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
